hadiths[139]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","It is narrated from the Chief of the Prophets, Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, that he said: ""Although we are the last of all nations, on the Day of Resurrection we will be the foremost. The only difference is that the Book was given to them before us, and to us after them. Thus, this (Friday) was also their day which was made obligatory upon them. (But) they differed concerning it, so Allah Almighty guided us to this day, and thus they followed us in it. The Jews will be (gathered) on the second day, and the Christians on the third day."
"2","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The example of me and the other prophets is like that of a person who built houses, and adorned and perfected them beautifully, but left a space for a brick at one of the corners of the houses. Now all the people come and walk around the building from all sides, and the building amazes them, but they also say: Why was a brick not placed here? By which the construction (of the building) would have been completed."" Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I am that brick."
"3","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The example of the miser and the one who gives charity is like two persons who are wearing two iron coats of mail or two armors, which reach up to their chests or collarbones. When the one who gives charity gives something in charity, it moves away from his body, and it covers his fingers, and (while walking) the mark of his feet disappears. And whenever the miser spends something or even intends in his heart to spend, every ring of that coat or armor tightens in its place. The miser tries to loosen it, but he cannot loosen it."
"4","And the Messenger (peace be upon him) said: ""My example is like that of a person who has kindled a fire. Then, when the surroundings are illuminated, moths and insects that usually fall into the fire begin to fall into it, and that person tries to stop them, but they overpower him and keep falling into the fire."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""So my example and yours is just like this: I want to grab you by your waists and save you from the fire (and I keep calling out), 'Save yourselves from the fire, save yourselves from the fire,' but you overpower me and keep plunging into the fire."
"5","And the Messenger (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, in Paradise there is a tree under whose shade a rider could travel for one hundred years and still not reach its end."
"6","And the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Beware of suspicion, beware of suspicion, for suspicion is often falsehood, and do not artificially raise prices over one another (without the intention to buy), and do not envy one another, and do not outbid one another out of selfishness, and do not create enmity among yourselves, and do not backbite one another, but rather, all of you are servants of Allah, so be brothers to one another."
"7","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""On Friday there is a moment in which, if any Muslim servant is standing in prayer and asks his Lord for something, Allah will surely grant him that thing."
"8","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The angels take turns among you by night and by day, and they gather at the prayers of Fajr and Asr. Then those angels who have stayed with you ascend, and Allah, though He knows best about His servants, asks them: ‘In what state did you leave My servants?’ They reply: ‘We left them while they were praying (Fajr), and when we came to them, they were praying (Asr).’”"
"9","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""As long as any one of you remains seated on his prayer place where he performed the prayer, and he does not lose his ablution, the angels continue to supplicate for mercy for him: O Allah! Forgive him, O Allah! Have mercy on him."
"10","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you says Ameen, and the angels also (at the same time) in the heavens (say Ameen), such that one’s Ameen coincides with the Ameen of the other, then all his previous sins will be forgiven."
"11","And Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said that once a man was driving a sacrificial animal on foot with a rope tied around its neck. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to him: ""Ride on it."" The man said: O Messenger of Allah! It is a sacrificial animal. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Woe to you! Ride on it, woe to you! Also ride on it."
"12","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him! If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little."
"13","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you strikes his brother, he should avoid the face."
"14","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""This fire of yours which the children of Adam kindle is one part out of seventy parts of the fire of Hell."" The people said: ""By Allah, O Messenger of Allah! Even this (fire of ours in this world) was quite enough (for the punishment of sinners)."" He, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: ""The fire of Hell is sixty-nine degrees hotter than this (worldly fire), and each degree is like the heat of this (worldly fire)."
"15","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When Allah Almighty created the creation, He wrote in His Book (the Preserved Tablet), which is with Him above the Throne, that: 'Indeed, My mercy prevails over My wrath.'"
"16","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Fasting is a shield, so if any one of you is fasting on a day, he should neither behave ignorantly nor speak obscenely. So if someone fights with him or abuses him, then he (the fasting person) should say (in response): I am fasting, I am fasting."
"17","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! The smell from the mouth of a fasting person is more beloved and purer to Allah than the fragrance of musk. (Allah Almighty says) The servant leaves his desires, his food, and his drink for My sake, so fasting is for Me and I alone will reward it."
"18","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""One of the prophets among the prophets stopped under the shade of a tree, where an ant bit him, so he ordered that all his belongings be moved from under the tree, then he had the ants burned with fire. Upon this, Allah the Exalted revealed to him that only one ant had bitten you, so you should have burned only that one."
"19","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul! If I did not fear hardship for the believers, I would never stay behind from any group fighting in the way of Allah. But I do not have enough means to mount all of them and take them with me, nor do they have enough mounts to ride with me, and nor do they like to stay behind after I have gone."
"20","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Every prophet has a supplication that is granted. So, if Allah wills, I wish to delay and postpone my supplication until the Day of Resurrection for the intercession of my ummah."
"21","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah also loves to meet him, and whoever does not like to meet Allah, Allah also does not like to meet him."
"22","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever obeys me has indeed obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. And whoever obeys the leader appointed by me has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys the leader has disobeyed me."
"23","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until wealth becomes abundant among you, so much so that it will overflow, to the extent that a wealthy person will worry about who will accept his zakat from him."" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""And knowledge will be taken away, and the time (of the Hour) will draw near, and tribulations will appear, and harj will become widespread."" The people asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is (harj)? He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Killing and bloodshed, killing and bloodshed."
"24","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until two great groups fight each other, and there will be a great battle between them, even though their claim will be one and the same."
"25","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until nearly thirty liars, Dajjals, appear; each one of them will think that he is the Messenger of Allah."
"26","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until the sun rises from the west. (Then after that) when it rises, the people will all believe upon seeing it, but this will be a stage when the faith of any soul will not benefit it. Because before this, neither had it accepted faith nor had it attained any good through its faith."
"27","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When the call to prayer (adhan) is made, Satan turns his back and flees, passing wind loudly so that he does not hear the sound of the adhan. When the call to prayer is finished, he returns. Then, when the iqamah for prayer is pronounced, he again turns his back and flees. When the iqamah is finished, he comes back and puts thoughts into the heart of the worshipper and says, 'Remember such-and-such, remember such-and-such,' things which he had not remembered before, until the worshipper does not remember how many (rak‘ahs) he has prayed."
"28","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah’s right hand is full, and continuous spending day and night does not diminish it. Just look! Since He created the heavens and the earth, how much has He spent? Yet what is in His right hand has not decreased at all."" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah’s Throne is upon the water, and in His other hand is the power to decrease and increase (things). He alone raises and lowers (things’ value)."
"29","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! Surely a day will come upon one of you in which he will not see me, then a time will come when seeing me will be more beloved to him than seeing his family and wealth."
"30","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Kisra, that is, the king of Persia, will be destroyed. After him, there will be no (other) Kisra. (Similarly) Caesar, that is, the king of Rome, will also be destroyed. After him, there will be no other Caesar. And surely you will spend the treasures of both of them in the way of Allah."" And the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, described war as deception."
"31","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah has said: I have prepared for My obedient servants such blessings as no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has ever conceived."
"32","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When I leave you (regarding something), then leave me (i.e., do not interfere unnecessarily in matters about which I show indifference). Indeed, the previous nations among you were destroyed because of their (unnecessary) questioning and their disagreements with their prophets. Therefore, when I forbid you from something, then avoid it, and when I command you to do something, then do it to the best of your ability."
"33","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When the call to prayer for the morning (Fajr) is given while one of you is in a state of major ritual impurity (junub), then he should not fast that day."
"34","And Abu al-Qasim (peace be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has ninety-nine names; whoever memorizes them will enter Paradise. And surely He (the Exalted) is Odd and loves the odd (number)."
"35","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any of you sees a person who is superior to him in wealth and appearance, then he should also look at the one who is lower than him in these qualities, due to which he has been given superiority over that person."
"36","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When a dog licks the utensil of any one of you, he should wash that utensil seven times (to purify it)."
"37","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! Indeed, I had firmly resolved to order my young men to collect bundles of wood for me, then I would order someone to lead the people in prayer, and then I would go to the houses (of those who did not join the congregational prayer) and burn them down along with their inhabitants."
"38","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When the strap or thong of one of your shoes breaks, do not walk with one shoe on and the other foot bare; rather, take off both shoes and walk with both feet bare."
"39","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “(Allah the Exalted says) The vow of the son of Adam does not give him anything except what I have already written in his destiny. Rather, the vow brings him to that which I have decreed for him. Through it, I extract wealth from the miser, and because of the vow, he gives Me as much as he could not have given Me before making the vow.”"
"40","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah Almighty has commanded me: (O My servant!) Spend your wealth in the way of goodness, and I will spend on you."" And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, called war deception and trickery."
"41","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Jesus, peace be upon him, saw a man stealing (so he said to him), 'Have you stolen?' The man replied, 'By no means, I swear by Him besides whom there is no true deity (I have not stolen).' So Jesus, peace be upon him, said: 'I believe in Allah, and (because of your oath) I consider my own eyes to be false.'"
"42","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I have been supported through awe, and I have been given concise speech."
"43","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Personally, I neither give you anything nor withhold anything from you. I am merely a treasurer; I dispose of wealth only where I have been commanded."
"44","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The imam is appointed so that he may be followed (in prayer); do not oppose him. Thus, when he says «اللہ أکبر» , you should say «اللہ أکبر» ; when he bows (in ruku‘), you should also bow; when he says «سمع اللہ لمن حمده» , you should (in response) say «اللهم ربنا لك الحمد» ; when he prostrates (in sujud), you should also prostrate; and when the imam prays sitting, you should also pray sitting."
"45","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Pay special attention to arranging the rows in prayer, for the beauty of prayer depends on the arrangement of the rows."
"46","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Once there was a dispute between Adam and Musa, peace be upon them. Musa, peace be upon him, said: Are you the Adam who led people astray and caused them to be expelled from Paradise and sent down to the earth? Adam, peace be upon him, said: Are you the Musa whom Allah granted knowledge of everything and, due to prophethood, gave superiority over other people? Musa, peace be upon him, replied: Yes! (I am he). Upon this, Adam, peace be upon him, said: Do you blame me for an act which Allah had written for me to do before my creation? In this way, Adam, peace be upon him, silenced Musa, peace be upon him."
"47","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Once, Ayub (peace be upon him) was bathing naked in his bathhouse when suddenly golden locusts began to fall upon him, so he started gathering them into his clothes."" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Upon this, his Lord, the Exalted, called out to Ayub (peace be upon him): 'O Ayub! Did We not make you independent of that which your eyes behold?' He replied: 'Yes, O my Lord! But I can never have enough of Your blessings.'"
"48","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The recitation of the Psalms was made easy and light for David, peace be upon him. He would order the saddle to be fastened on his mount, and before the saddle was fastened, he would complete the recitation (of the Psalms). And he used to eat only from what he earned with his own hands."
"49","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The dream of a righteous man is one forty-sixth part of prophethood."
"50","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The younger should greet the elder, the passerby should greet those who are sitting, and the smaller group should greet the larger group."
"51","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I will continue to fight the people until they declare «لا إله إلا اللہ» (there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah). So when they declare it, they have protected their wealth and their lives from me, except for its due right (i.e., retribution, apostasy, or any other prescribed legal punishment is excepted), and their reckoning is with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."
"52","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “There was a debate between Paradise and Hell. Hell said: Because of the arrogant and proud people, I have superiority over you. Paradise said: What is it that only the weak, lowly, and simple-minded people enter me instead of the arrogant? Upon this, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said to Paradise: You are My mercy; through you I bestow My mercy upon whomever I wish among My servants. And He said to Hell: You are My punishment; through you I punish whomever I wish among My servants. And the filling of both of you (according to your measure) is a reality. However, Hell will only be filled when Allah places His foot in it. (When Allah places His foot in it), Hell will say: Enough! Enough! (Thus) at that time it will be filled and it will contract, and Allah will not wrong any one of His creation. And as for the filling of Paradise, for that Allah will create another creation.”"
"53","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you performs istinja with stones, he should use an odd number of stones."
"54","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, says that when My servant intends to do a good deed, (merely by his intention, as long as he does not act upon it) I write one good deed (in his record of deeds), and when he acts upon that heartfelt intention, I write ten good deeds (in his record of deeds) for him. And when (My servant) intends to commit a bad deed, (merely by his intention to do a bad deed) I forgive him, that is, as long as he does not commit the bad deed, and when he commits (that) deed, I write (only) the like of that evil (just one sin) for him.”"
"55","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Allah! For any one of you, a place in Paradise as small as the space taken by a whip is better than all that is between the heavens and the earth."
"56","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, for the least of you whose dwelling is prepared in Paradise, it will be said: Wish! So he will make many wishes, then he will be asked: Have you wished? He will reply: Yes! Then it will be said to him: Surely, for you is the like of your wishes and as much more besides."
"57","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If it were not for the virtue of migration, I would certainly have been one of the Ansar, and if people were to walk in a mountain pass or a valley and the Ansar were to walk in another mountain pass, I would walk with the Ansar in their mountain pass."
"58","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If it were not for the Children of Israel, food would not spoil and meat would not rot, and if it were not for Hawwa (Eve), no woman would ever betray her husband."
"59","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah Almighty created Adam, peace be upon him, in his image; his height was sixty cubits. So when Allah Almighty had created him, He commanded him: Go to that group, meaning the group of angels who were sitting there, greet them with salam, and listen carefully to the words they say in reply to your salam, for that will be your way of greeting and the way of your descendants."" He, peace be upon him, said: ""Then he went and said to the angels «السلام علیکم» , and they replied «وعلیکم السلام ورحمة اللہ» , and the angels added «ورحمة اللہ» in their reply."" He, peace be upon him, said: ""Every person who enters Paradise will be in the form of Adam, peace be upon him; his height will be sixty cubits. Since then, the stature of mankind has been decreasing continuously."
"60","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The Angel of Death came to Musa, peace be upon him, and said: Fulfill the command of your Lord (i.e., surrender your soul to the Creator). Upon this, Musa, peace be upon him, struck the angel on the eye and gouged out his eye. The angel returned to the presence of Allah and said: Indeed, You have sent me to a servant of Yours who does not want to die, and he has gouged out my eye. So Allah restored his eye and said: Go back to My servant and say to him: Do you wish to remain alive? If you truly wish to remain alive, then place your hand on the back of an ox; for every hair your hand covers, you will live one year for each hair. Musa, peace be upon him, asked: Then what will happen? The angel said: Then you will die. Musa, peace be upon him, said: Then it is better that I die now. Then he prayed: O my Lord! Bring me close to the Holy Land by the distance of a stone’s throw.” (Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, says that) the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If I were there, I would certainly show you the grave of Musa, peace be upon him, which is by the side of the road near a red sand hill.”"
"61","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Children of Israel used to bathe naked in such a way that they would see each other's private parts, but Musa (Moses), peace be upon him, used to bathe alone. Upon this, they said: By Allah! Nothing prevents Musa, peace be upon him, from bathing with us except that he is suffering from swelling of the testicles."
"62","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Abundance of worldly goods is not true wealth; rather, true wealth is the richness of the heart."
"63","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, delaying repayment by a wealthy person is injustice, and when your debt is transferred to a wealthy person, then seek the debt from him."
"64","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the worst and most detested person in the sight of Allah will be the one who is called 'Shahanshah' (King of Kings) in the world. There is no Shahanshah except Allah."
"65","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A man was walking arrogantly in two garments, and he was overcome with self-conceit, so (by the command of Allah) he was caused to sink into the earth, and he will remain (in that state) until the Day of Resurrection."
"66","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I am as My servant thinks of Me; as he thinks of Me, so I am with him."
"67","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Every child is born upon the fitrah (the upright religion), then his parents make him a Jew or a Christian. Just as among your cattle, a young one is born—do you find any among them with a cut ear? Rather, you yourselves cut its ear."" The noble Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, asked: O Messenger of Allah! Tell us about the children who die in childhood. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah knows best what they would have done."
"68","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is a bone in a human being which the earth never consumes; from that bone, people will be recreated on the Day of Resurrection."" The Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! Which bone is that?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""It is the backbone."
"69","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Refrain from continuous fasting (without breaking the fast), refrain from continuous fasting."" The companions, may Allah be pleased with them, said: O Messenger of Allah! You yourself observe continuous fasting. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I am not like you in this matter. I spend the night in such a state that my Lord feeds me and gives me drink. So you should only bear as much hardship in deeds as you have strength for."
"70","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you wakes up from sleep, he should not put his hand into the water for ablution before washing it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"71","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Every day on which the sun rises, charity is due on every joint of a person."" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""To act justly between two people is charity, to help a man mount his riding animal, or to load his belongings onto it, is charity, and good words are charity."" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Every step taken towards prayer is also a charity, and removing something harmful from the road is also charity."
"72","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever does not pay the zakat of his animals, on the Day of Resurrection those very animals will be set upon him, trampling his face harshly with their hooves."
"73","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the treasure of one of you (from which he did not give zakat) will take the form of a bald snake, and the owner of the treasure will run away from it, but the bald snake will keep following him and will say: I am your treasure."" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Allah, I swear by Allah! That snake will keep chasing him continuously, until that person stretches out his hand and the snake will swallow it."
"74","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Do not urinate in standing water, for then you may perform ablution from it."
"75","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The one who goes door to door, making rounds among people, and who returns with a morsel or two, or a date or two, is not a true needy person. Rather, the real needy person is the one who does not possess enough wealth to fulfill his needs, feels ashamed to ask people, and whose poverty is not apparent so that charity may be given to him."
"76","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""No woman should observe (optional) fasting in the presence of her husband without his permission, nor allow anyone to enter his house without his permission. (However,) if she spends anything from his earnings without his permission, half of the reward for that spending will go to her husband."
"77","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""None of you should wish for death, nor should he pray for it before it comes, because when any of you dies, his (means of) deeds come to an end. Surely, the life of a believer only increases him in goodness."
"78","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""None of you should call grapes «كرم» (honor and generosity), because «كرم» (that) is only a Muslim man."
"79","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A man bought land from another man, and the buyer found a pot of gold in that land. So the buyer said to the owner of the land: 'Take your gold from me, for I bought the land from you, not the gold.' Upon this, the seller of the land said: 'I sold you the land and whatever was in it.' Then both of them took their case to a third person. The judge asked them: 'Do you have children?' One of them said: 'I have a son.' And the other said: 'I have a daughter.' The judge said: 'Marry the two to each other, and spend some of the gold on yourselves and them, and give some in charity.'"
"80","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If any one of you were to lose his mount and then find it, would he be happy?"" The companions, may Allah be pleased with them, replied: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)! Allah is far more pleased with the repentance of His servant than you are when you find your lost mount."
"81","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, Allah the Exalted says: When My servant draws near to Me by a handspan, I draw near to him by a cubit (an arm's length); when he draws near to Me by a cubit, I draw near to him by two arm's lengths; and when My servant comes to Me walking, I come to him running (or he said: I come to him swiftly)."
"82","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you performs ablution, let him draw water into his nostrils and then expel it."
"83","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him! If I had gold equal to the mountain of Uhud, I would like that not three nights pass before I give it away, and that I do not leave with myself even a single dinar, except that I keep something to pay off a debt."
"84","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When the cook brings food to you, who has spared you from the heat and smoke of the food, then invite him to eat with you, otherwise place a few morsels in his hand."
"85","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""None of you should say: 'Give drink to your ""Rabb"" (lord/master), feed your ""Rabb"", or give ablution to your ""Rabb"",' and no one should call (his master) 'my Rabb', but rather he should call (his master) 'Sayyidi wa Mawlaya'—my chief, my master. It is not proper for anyone to say 'Abdi'—my slave, or 'Amati'—my female slave, rather he should say: 'Ghulami'—my servant, my maidservant, my slave."
"86","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The first group to enter Paradise will have faces like the full moon on the fourteenth night. They (the people of Paradise) will neither spit in it, nor blow their noses, nor relieve themselves. Their vessels and combs will be of gold and silver. Their incense burners will be of aloes-wood (oud al-Hindi). Their sweat will be fragrant like musk, and each person of Paradise will have two wives, whose marrow of the shins will be visible due to their beauty through the flesh. There will be no disagreement or hatred among the people of Paradise; their hearts will be like the heart of a single person, and they will glorify Allah morning and evening."
"87","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""O Allah! I make a covenant with You, which You will never break. I am but a human being, so if I have caused harm to any believer, or spoken harshly to him, or punished him, or cursed him, then make all of this a means of mercy, purification, and nearness for him, by which You bring him close to Yourself on the Day of Resurrection."
"88","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The spoils of war were not permissible for the nations before us, but Allah, seeing our weakness and helplessness, made this wealth lawful and pure for us."
"89","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A woman entered Hell because of the crime of confining her cat; she neither fed it nor set it free so that it could eat the insects of the earth, until it became weak and died."
"90","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A thief is not a believer at the time of stealing, an adulterer is not a believer at the time of committing adultery, and a drunkard is not a believer at the time of drinking alcohol. By the One in whose hand is the life of Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him! If any honorable person among you commits robbery, to whom the believers look up, then at the time of that robbery, he is not a believer. And the one who betrays trust is not a believer at the time of committing betrayal. So you must abstain from these (evil and despicable habits)! Beware."
"91","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! Whoever from this Ummah, whether he be a Jew or a Christian, hears of my Prophethood and dies without believing in the religion with which I have been sent, he will be among the inhabitants of Hellfire."
"92","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If any matter arises during the prayer, it is prescribed for men to say «سبحان اللہ» and for women to clap."
"93","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Any wound that a Muslim receives in the way of Allah will appear on the Day of Resurrection in the same state as when it was inflicted, blood will be flowing from it, its color will be like that of blood, and its fragrance will be like that of musk."
"94","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When I return to my house, I find a date lying on my bed (in my house), and I pick it up to eat it, but then, fearing that it might be from charity, I throw it away."
"95","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""You will continue to ask questions in this manner until one of you says: 'This is Allah who created all of creation, but who created Allah?'"
"96","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By Allah! For any one of you to persist in severing ties with his family due to an oath is a greater sin in the sight of Allah than (breaking the oath and) offering the expiation which Allah has made obligatory upon him."
"97","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When two men are compelled to take an oath and both of them prefer to take the oath, then cast lots between them."
"98","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you buys a «مصراة» (an animal whose milk has been retained in its udders) she-camel or goat, after milking it, he has the choice of two options: if he wishes, he may keep it, or if he wishes, he may return it, and in exchange for the milk he has milked, he should give the owner a «صاع» of dates."
"99","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""An old man remains young in two things: first, in hoping and wishing for a long life; second, in desiring abundance of wealth."
"100","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""None of you should point a weapon at his brother, (because) he does not know that perhaps Satan may cause the weapon to slip from his hand (and he may kill someone), as a result of which he (the killer) will fall into a pit of Hell."
"101","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah became extremely angry with the people who did this to His Messenger,"" while at that time the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was pointing towards his four blessed front teeth (which had been martyred)."
"102","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah became extremely angry with the people whom the Messenger of Allah killed in the way of Allah."
"103","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""A portion of adultery has been decreed for the son of Adam, which he will inevitably encounter. The adultery of the eye is looking (at what is forbidden), and its confirmation is averting the gaze (if a person turns away after the first glance and lowers his eyes upon seeing what is forbidden, then this is a true gaze, otherwise not). The adultery of the tongue is speaking (obscenely), the adultery of the heart is wishing and desiring, and the private parts either confirm or deny (the act of) sin."
"104","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you makes his Islam good (through righteousness and obedience), then every good deed that he performs is written for him as ten to seven hundred times (its reward), and every sin that he commits is written as only one sin. This continues until he meets Allah, the Exalted."
"105","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any of you leads the people in prayer, he should make it brief, for among the congregation are some who are elderly, some who are weak, and some who are ill. But if he prays alone, he may prolong the prayer as much as he wishes."
"106","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The angels say: O Lord! Your (such-and-such) servant intends to commit an evil deed. Although Allah Almighty knows this very well. Allah Almighty says: Watch over him; if he commits the evil deed, then write one evil for him, and if he refrains from it, then write one good deed for him, because this servant has refrained from the evil out of fear of Me."
"107","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah Almighty has said that My servant has denied Me, though it does not befit him, and My servant has abused Me, though it is not appropriate for him. (In any case) his denying Me is that he says: Allah will never resurrect us again as He created us at first. And his abusing Me is that he says: Allah has taken a son, though I am self-sufficient; I have no offspring, nor was I begotten, and there is none comparable to Me."
"108","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Perform the prayer at a cooler time during the heat, for the intensity of the heat is from the steam of Hell."
"109","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you becomes without ablution, his prayer is not accepted until he performs ablution."
"110","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When the call to prayer is given, come to the prayer with calmness and tranquility. Then whatever part of the prayer you catch, perform it, and whatever you miss, complete it (afterwards)."
"111","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah Almighty smiles at two men, one of whom will be the killer of the other, (yet) both will enter Paradise."" Upon this, the companions, may Allah be pleased with them, asked: O Messenger of Allah! How is that? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""(It is) that the one who fought in the way of Allah was martyred and entered Paradise. Then Allah granted the other, that is, the killer, the ability to repent and guided him to accept Islam. Then he also fought in the way of Allah and was martyred."
"112","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""None of you should make a deal over the deal of his brother, nor should he send a proposal over the proposal of his brother."
"113","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The disbeliever eats with seven intestines, and the believer eats with one intestine."
"114","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Khidr was named «خضر» because once he sat on white sand or dry land, and suddenly that land beneath him turned lush and green, waving with vegetation."
"115","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Surely Allah, the Exalted, will not look (with mercy) on the Day of Resurrection at the one who lets his lower garment hang below the ankles."
"116","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Children of Israel were commanded to enter the door in a state of prostration and to say (along with it), '(O Allah!) Forgive us' (so that all your sins may be forgiven), but they altered it. So instead of prostrating, they entered the door dragging themselves on their buttocks, and instead of saying «حطة» , they said «حبة في شعيرة» (which means wheat)."
"117","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any one of you stands for the night prayer and the Qur'an becomes entangled on his tongue, and he does not understand what he is reciting, then he should lie down (and sleep)."
"118","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah Almighty has said that the son of Adam should not say: 'Woe to the times,' for I am the Time (the Creator), and I alone send forth the night and the day continuously, and when I will, I shall withhold them both."
"119","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""How excellent is that slave whom Allah causes to depart from this world while obeying his Lord and his master in the best manner; this is very good for him, this is very good for him."
"120","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When any of you stands for prayer, he should not spit in front of him, because as long as he is in his place of prayer, he is engaged in intimate discourse with Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. And likewise, he should not spit to his right side, because there is an angel on his right. Yes, (if he wishes to spit) he should spit to his left side or under his foot, then cover it."
"121","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""On the day of Friday (during the sermon), your saying to the people 'Be quiet' while they are talking among themselves is an idle and vain thing."
"122","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""According to the Book of Allah, I am closer to the believers than other people. So, whoever among you dies leaving behind a debt or dependents, then call me and I will take care of them. And whoever dies leaving behind wealth, then his heirs will have priority over it, whoever they may be."
"123","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""None of you should supplicate in this manner: 'O Allah! If You will, forgive me; if You will, have mercy on me; or if You will, provide for me.' Rather, he should ask with full certainty, for Allah does whatever He wills, and there is none to compel Him."
"124","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “One of the prophets from among the previous prophets prepared for battle, and he said to his people: No one should follow me who has married and desires to spend the night with his wife but has not yet been alone with her, nor should anyone follow me who has built a house but has not yet put a roof on it, nor should anyone go who has bought pregnant goats or pregnant camels and is waiting for them to give birth. Then that prophet fought in battle, and when he reached a town at the time of Asr prayer or near Asr, that prophet said to the sun: ‘You are also bound by the command of Allah, and I am also bound by the command of Allah.’ (Then he prayed to Allah:) O Allah! Hold back the sun for a while for my sake. Then the sun was held back until Allah granted them victory. Then the people gathered the spoils of war, and when they had collected them, a fire came to consume (burn) the spoils, but it refused to consume them. At this, that prophet said: Someone among you has committed treachery (with the spoils). Therefore, one man from each tribe should pledge allegiance on my hand. When the pledges began, the hand of one man clung to the hand of that prophet. So the prophet said: The man who committed treachery is among your tribe, so now your whole tribe should pledge allegiance on my hand. So they pledged allegiance, and then the hands of two or three men clung to the hand of the prophet. The prophet said: Treachery has been committed by the people of your tribe. Eventually, they brought forth gold equal to the head of a cow (which had been stolen from the spoils) and placed it among the spoils. Then the fire came and consumed that wealth. (In the end) the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ‘The spoils of war were not lawful for those before us. But Allah, considering our weakness and humility, made this wealth lawful for us.’”"
"125","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Once I was sleeping, I saw in a dream that I was drawing water from a cistern and giving it to people to drink. Then Abu Bakr came to me and, to give me relief, took the bucket from my hand and drew two buckets of water, but there was some weakness in his drawing. May Allah forgive him."" He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Then Umar ibn al-Khattab came to me and took the bucket from him, and no one could draw water as he did. People drank until they were satisfied, and the cistern was overflowing."
"126","The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight 'Jawr Kerman', which is a non-Arab nation. Their faces will be red, their eyes small, and their noses flat. Their faces will be like hammered shields."
"127","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The Hour will not be established until you fight a people whose shoes will be made of hair."
"128","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Pride and arrogance are found among those who keep horses and camels, and seriousness and dignity are found among those who herd goats."
"129","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I think that people, in this matter of leadership, follow the Quraysh. The Muslims follow the Muslim Quraysh, and the disbelievers follow the disbelieving Quraysh."
"130","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The best women among those who ride camels are the women of Quraysh, who are extremely compassionate towards their children in their early years and are very protective of their husbands' wealth."
"131","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The effect of the evil eye is real."" And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade «وشم» , that is, applying kohl by adoption."
"132","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Any one of you remains in prayer as long as the prayer keeps him, and nothing prevents him from leaving the prayer except waiting for it."
"133","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The upper hand is better than the lower hand. And begin charity with your close relatives."
"134","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I am the closest of all people to Jesus son of Mary, peace be upon him, in this world and the Hereafter."" The noble companions, may Allah be pleased with them, asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! How is that?"" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""(All) the prophets are paternal brothers; their mothers are different, but their religion is one. So there is no prophet between us two."
"135","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Once I was sleeping when the treasures of the earth were presented to me, and two gold bangles were placed in my hands. They weighed heavily upon me and caused me great distress, then it was revealed to me that I should blow on them, so I blew and they (both) flew away. I interpreted this dream to mean that I am between two liars, one from Sana'a and the other from Yamamah."
"136","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""None among you will be saved by his deeds alone. Therefore, remain steadfast on the right path and stay as close to it as possible."" The Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! Will your deeds also not be the cause of your salvation?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: ""I too will not attain salvation through my deeds, unless Allah, the Exalted, covers me with His grace and mercy (that is a different matter)."
"137","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade two ways of buying and selling and two ways of wearing clothes: (The prohibited ways of wearing clothes are these) that none of you should wrap himself in a single garment in such a way that his private parts are not covered with cloth, and when he prays (in a single sheet), he should wrap it in such a manner that both ends of the sheet are tied on his neck from opposite sides. And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade making a sale by touching the goods, or by throwing a pebble, and from «بیع بخش» (brokerage sale)."
"138","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is no compensation for an animal that is wounded (or killed), for falling into a well and being injured, nor for dying by falling into fire. And one-fifth of the buried treasure (is for Allah and His Messenger, peace and blessings be upon him)."
"139","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When you go to any town and stay there,"" I think then he said: ""then your share will be in that town or it will be your property."" Or something similar to this. ""And whichever town (people) disobey Allah and His Messenger, then in the case of victory, one fifth of it is for Allah and His Messenger, then that too is for you."
